vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
Enforce configuration invariants when deactivating a manager:
- In `updatePositionManager`/`togglePositionManagerStatus`, if `managerId == defaultManagerId` and the operation would set `isActive=false`, then require `shouldExecuteAllocation == false` OR require `defaultManagerId` is changed first.
Example:
```solidity
if (managerId == defaultManagerId && !newIsActive && shouldExecuteAllocation) {
  revert LiquidityBuffer__InvalidConfiguration();
}
```
Alternatively, automatically select a new active default manager before deactivation, or disable auto-allocation in the same transaction.
